          </p>
          <p
            style="margin-bottom: 8px;"
          >
            <strong>
              Mature cards
            </strong>
             — cards with a stability above 30 days. They need reviewing less and less often.
          </p>
          <p
            style="margin-bottom: 8px;"
          >
            <strong>
              Recall accuracy
            </strong>
             — the share of reviews rated Good or Easy in the last 30 days.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>
              Critical cards
            </strong>
             — cards you've flagged as high-stakes. Reviewed at higher priority.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div
      class="rapp-card rapp-mb16"
    >
      <div
        style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 8px;"
      >
        How scheduling works
      </div>
      <div
        style="font-size: 13px; color: rgb(58, 82, 70); line-height: 1.75;"
      >
        <p
          style="margin-bottom: 8px;"
        >
          Nidus estimates how likely you are to recall each card, then schedules it just before that probability drops below your target (default: 90%). Cards you know well drift out to months; cards you find hard come back in days.
        </p>
        <p>
          Reference: Open Spaced Repetition project, github.com/open-spaced-repetition.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div
      class="rapp-card rapp-mb20"
    >
      <div
        style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 8px;"
      >
        What the first few months look like
      </div>
      <div
        style="display: flex; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; font-size: 12px; color: rgb(58, 82, 70);"
      >
        <div>
          <strong>
            Week 1
          </strong>
           — short intervals, high volume. Nidus is learning your memory patterns.
        </div>
        <div>
          <strong>
            Week 4
          </strong>
           — familiar cards space out to 1–3 weeks. Daily load starts to settle.
        </div>
        <div>
          <strong>
            Month 3
          </strong>
           — well-known cards reviewed monthly. New cards drive most of the workload.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div
      style="opacity: 0.25; filter: blur(2px); pointer-events: none;"
    >
      <div
        class="rapp-stat-row rapp-mb20"
        data-testid="headline-stats"
      >
        <div
          class="rapp-stat-box"
        >
          <div
            class="rapp-stat-num"
            data-testid="stat-reviews-today"
            style="color: rgb(74, 107, 92);"
          >
